cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Q-Matrix: A Multi-Agent System for Automated Curriculum Concept-Skill Mapping"
abstract: >-
  Q-Matrix is a multi-agent system that turns raw curriculum documentation into
  validated, prerequisite-mapped curriculum CSVs. A thin orchestrator coordinates
  eleven single-responsibility LLM agents — extraction, generation, evaluation,
  revision, surgical repair, selection, and multi-level prerequisite mapping —
  with a human in the loop only on escalation. This repository is the code layer;
  curriculum data lives in a separate knowledge-base repository.
authors:
  - family-names: Tamboli
    given-names: Shrideep
    affiliation: AI Ready School
  - family-names: Maddala
    given-names: Chiranjeevi
    affiliation: AI Ready School
repository-code: "https://github.com/MaximusTitan/q-matrix-agents"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-24"
keywords:
  - curriculum-mapping
  - multi-agent-systems
  - large-language-models
  - education-technology
  - knowledge-graph
  - prerequisite-relations

